{"id":260921833914672,"type":"album","name":"Ege Bamyasi","artist":"Can","year":1972,"weight":10,"info":{"yt":"BP6Tm0vYGQk","cover":"https://lastfm-img.freetls.fastly.net/i/u/300x300/8ad03182ab4e49cf8a39164a9c36c994.jpg"},"artist_ref":{"id":126657727149758,"name":"The Can","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Can_1972_%28Heinrich_Klaffs_Collection_102%29.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[],"lists":[],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"Another masterpiece that continued the avant-garde and experimental direction of \"Tago Mago\" but achieved greater accessibility due to the consistent rhythmic presence throughout the album, particularly highlighting Jaki Liebezeit's exceptional drumming. This album offered a funkier, extremely precise, and polished rhythm, continuously propelled by Holger Czukay's pulsating and repetitive bass. Damo Suzuki shone on this record as one of his generation's most unique and brilliant vocalists, with his singing on \"Sing Swan Song\" notably influencing Kanye West's track \"Drunk and Hot Girls\" and countless rock artists. \"Este disco nos ofrece una rímica más funky, extremadamente precisa y pulida, se os tenía constantemente por el bajo pulsante, repetitivo de Chukai.\"","year":1972,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Central Sonora","episode":"CAN ｜ La Banda que (posiblemente) Inspiró a tu banda preferida","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4qHiw2wHWAI"}]}],"book_tracks":[{"id":260921833914672,"artist":"Can","artist_id":126657727149758,"title":"Ege Bamyasi","year":1972,"ess":1,"yt":"BP6Tm0vYGQk","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Kosmische Musik y krautrock","scene_id":107234531659708,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#kosmische","chapters":["Sección 3.7"],"pages":[[1,66,null]]}],"others":[{"id":219651823668291,"type":"album","name":"Tago Mago","year":1971